  "question": {
    "text": "The part of a circuit shown in the figure consists of two ideal diodes and a few resistors. The equivalent resistance of the circuit between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0053_5db665a3be2a.jpg\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 122px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>13</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> or <math><mn>13</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> or zero",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math>, both the junction diodes are forward biased and the given circuit diagram becomes a balanced Wheatstone bridge. The equivalent resistance, in this case, becomes <math><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.<br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math>, the diodes are reverse biased. In that case,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> are in series."
  }
